; C10  Winning 42 p. 24 (W42-p024-b)
; Rule, as the gate reads it: on the first trick, a bidder with exactly one off
; and four or more trumps leads the off.
; What the book says, in our words: leading the off before trumps is
; reasonable on trick one only in that shape, and dangerous otherwise. That is
; a permission, not an instruction: in Hand 14 (p. 28, W42-p028-b) the bidder
; holds that shape and leads trump. The gate reads it as an instruction; so
; does this file, to encode the gate; tests/book.rs records the difference.
; Python gate (pour_bidder gate_c10, "C10-gate: off lead"): bidder, trick 1,
; one off and four or more trumps; the book's tiles are the offs. An off is a
; non-trump tile some tile outside the hand outranks in the suit it leads.
; How this encoding differs: none from the gate.
(policy c10-off-on-trick-one
  (fallback lowest-legal)
  (rule lead-the-off (select answer)
    (guard
      (query
        (roles
          (chair b)
          (domino off) (domino over) (context suit)
          (domino t1) (domino t2) (domino t3) (domino t4))
        (out off)
        (pattern
          (viewer b)
          (declarer b)
          (trick-number 1)
          (next-actor b)
          (own-legal t1) (in t1 q*)
          (own-legal t2) (in t2 q*)
          (own-legal t3) (in t3 q*)
          (own-legal t4) (in t4 q*)
          (own-legal off)
          (not (in off q*))
          (leads-context off suit)
          (live over)
          (not (own-legal over))
          (in over suit)
          (beats over off suit)
          (none (roles (domino second) (domino above) (context its))
            (own-legal second) (not (tile second off)) (not (in second q*)) (leads-context second its)
            (live above) (not (own-legal above)) (in above its) (beats above second its)))))))
